FFmpeg 9.0: Respect Vulkan decode-image and synchronization requirements

Generic Vulkan format capabilities do not establish support for the same usage
and creation flags on video-profile-bound images. Omit storage usage on decode
output and restrict image usage and flags to those reported for the selected
profile. Require decode and GPU-copy usage while negotiating optional sampling
support. Consumers must copy output without sampling or mutable plane views
on the GPU before rendering. Dedicated DPB and DRM modifier allocations are
unchanged.

Keep 64-bit access flags in execution bookkeeping. Cover previous reads/writes
and layout transitions when reusing decoder output and reference images, with
all-command semaphore stages to synchronize uses on other queues.

